.TH PKG-REMOVE 1 "2026-08-07" "pkg-remove.sh" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pkg-remove.sh \- interactive package remover (fzf TUI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkg-remove.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkg-remove.sh
is an interactive
.BR fzf (1)
front end for removing installed packages. It takes no command\-line
arguments; the whole workflow happens inside the fzf list and its preview
pane.
.P
On start, the script lists every installed package (\fBpacman \-Qq\fR,
bare package names) and feeds it to
.BR fzf (1).
Filter by typing, toggle entries into the selection with
.B Tab
and press Enter. The chosen package names are collected and removed in a
single call to
.BR paru (1)
(\fBparu \-Rns \-\-noconfirm\fR), which removes each package together with
its unneeded dependencies and configuration files, without asking for
confirmation. If the selection is empty (the list is dismissed), the
script exits silently without removing anything.
.P
A wrap\-enabled preview pane at the bottom (65% of the screen) shows
detailed information for the highlighted package via
.BR pacman (8)
(\fBpacman \-Qii\fR), falling back to
.BR yay (1)
(\fByay \-Qii\fR) for packages unknown to pacman; the preview command uses
field \fB{1}\fR, the package name. Because the action is destructive, the
pointer and multi\-select marker are shown in red, and the preview label
reads:
.IP
\fBalt\-p: toggle preview | alt\-j/k: scroll preview | tab: multi\-select\fR
.SS Key bindings
.IP \(bu 2
.B Tab
toggle multi\-selection of the current entry
.IP \(bu 2
.B Ctrl-J
move the cursor down the list
.IP \(bu 2
.B Ctrl-K
move the cursor up the list
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-P
toggle the preview pane
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-D
scroll the preview half a page down
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-U
scroll the preview half a page up
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-J
scroll the preview one line down
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-K
scroll the preview one line up
.P
The script requires
.BR fzf (1)
and
.BR paru (1);
the installed\-package list and preview use
.BR pacman (8).
.SH EXAMPLES
Remove one or more installed packages:
.IP
.EX
pkg-remove.sh
.EE
.P
Type a search term to filter, press
.B Tab
on each package to remove, then press Enter to uninstall all of them with
their unneeded dependencies.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paru (1),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR pkg-install (1),
.BR pkg-install-aur (1)
